        "title": "Heather Morgan",
        "source": "kg"
      }
    },
    {
      "node_id": "kg_doc_12",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Los Vendidos (Spanish for The Sold Ones or The Sellouts) is a one-act play by Chicano playwright Luis Valdez, a founding member of El Teatro Campesino. He wrote it in 1967, and it was first performed at the Brown Beret junta in Elysian Park, East Los Angeles. The play examines stereotypes of Latinos in California and how they are treated by local, state, and federal governments.",
      "depth": 0,
      "parent_id": null,
      "value": 0.25,
      "temperature": 0.25,
      "expanded": false,
      "visit_count": 0,
      "persistent": true,
